{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The portable Samsung SSD feels useful for backing up photos and files from the memory cards I already use, without requiring a computer upgrade.",
    "The compact Samsung USB flash drive fits my interest in small, practical storage accessories and gives me a convenient way to transfer files."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The internal SSDs and enclosure assume I am upgrading a computer or repurposing a drive; my memory-card purchases do not indicate that need.",
    "The Blink cameras serve home surveillance, while my tripods, film, and lens cap relate to photography.",
    "The Echo displays and keyboard do not solve a current accessory need. Buying a Fire tablet does not mean I want another display, an Alexa service, or a replacement keyboard."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in removable storage seems to have been stretched into interest in any storage hardware, even products requiring installation or compatibility checks.",
    "My tablet and photography purchases seem to have been treated as broad interest in smart-home devices and electronics."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "I repeatedly buy accessories with specific practical jobs: reading and organizing memory cards, mounting devices, charging equipment, and protecting lenses.",
    "Compatibility matters to me: my history includes accessories for particular connectors, device sizes, and lens dimensions. A related product is useful only if it works with equipment I own.",
    "Frequent electronics purchases do not mean I am currently starting a computer-building or home-security project."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my interest in practical storage, but extended it too broadly into computer upgrades and smart-home devices."
}"}
